LCP:::9.2.6.9.content:
Plume

Wastes with a high moisture content, such as poultry litter, are prone to visible plume formation. There are three generic techniques for conditioning exhaust gases to prevent visible plume formation from the stack:

exhaust gas reheating;
exhaust gas condensation;
flue-gas temperature control.

Condensation techniques produce large volumes of liquid for disposal, which can be contaminated by polluting substances and may require neutralisation.

