Under the generic denomination of manure additives is a group of products made up of different compounds that interact with the manure, changing its characteristics and properties. The following positive effects are claimed and are described to different degrees in the label of every product:

a reduction in the emission of several gaseous compounds (NH3 and H2S);
a reduction of unpleasant odours;
