Poultry farms

As regards layer farms, artificial heating of the housing is not commonly applied, due to the low temperature needs of the birds and the relatively high stocking density. Activities requiring energy are:

heating the water in winter;
feed distribution;
housing ventilation;
lighting, this requires high consumption levels in order to artificially maintain a constant period of high light levels during the year, so as to increase egg production during the periods of the shortest days;

