Temperature control

The temperature in poultry houses is controlled by means of the following techniques:

insulation of the building;
local heating (deep litter systems) or space heating;
direct heating (e.g. infrared, gas/air heating, gas convectors, hot-air cannon) or indirect heating (central heating of space, central heating of underfloor);
