Feeding systems

Feeding practices depend on the type of production and bird species. Feed is given in mashed form, crumbs, or pellets. Layers are generally fed ad libitum  . Meat species, such as broilers and turkeys, are also fed ad libitum. Hand feeding is still applied, but in large enterprises modern feeding systems are applied that reduce the spillage of feed and that allow accurate (phase) feeding. 

