Ventilation of pig housing

Animal houses have to be ventilated in order to :

supply the animals with fresh air;
dissipate excess heat in order to keep the temperature within the optimal animal-specific range, which depends on age and performance;
remove gaseous substances and dust;
avoid damage to buildings due to humidity.


