A proper management of manure landspreading takes account of the nutrient balance (see Section 4.13.1), as well as surface water and groundwater protection schemes (see Section 4.13.2). It combines the following aspects:

application on suitable areas;
defining and observing buffer zones;
proper timing of application; 
defining of spreading rate (in relation to nutrient content).

