FDM:::16.9.content:
Malting

Malt is made from malting-grade cereals, usually barley or wheat, although occasionally other cereals such as rye and oats may be used. There are five product groups:

white malts (malted barley, malted wheat, malted oats, malted sorghum, high enzymatic malt); 
peated or smoked malt;
coloured malts (such as crystal and caramel malts);
roasted malts (range including both light and dark roasts); 
roasted barley. 

