Overview

From the bright beer tanks, the beer is pumped to the packaging area where most beer is bottled, canned or kegged.

During this final operation, it is important that: 

the beer is prevented from coming into contact with oxygen to protect the fresh taste of beer;
no carbon dioxide is lost as the beer is carbonated to certain specifications during its processing;
microbiological contamination of the product is prevented; this may require treatment and disinfection of the water;
the pack

