Optimisation of batch dyeing

Description
Optimisation of batch dyeing includes techniques such as:

maintaining a constant and low liquor ratio;
separating the exhausted dye bath and the rinsing water;
mechanical or pneumatic extraction of the liquor from the fabric;
shortening the dyeing cycle, e.g. by draining and filling baths with pumps, by using tanks to prepare the liquor in parallel with an ongoing cycle, using cooling water for rinsing;
