TXT:::2.11.1.content:
Washing with water

Important factors in washing are:

water characteristics;
choice of soaps and detergents;
hydromechanical action;
temperature and pH;
rinsing stage.

Washing is normally carried out in hot water (40-100 degC) in the presence of a wetting agent and a detergent. The detergent emulsifies the mineral oils and disperses the undissolved pigments. The choice of the surfactants may also vary depending on the type of fibre. Mixtures of anionic and non-ionic surfactants are commonly us

TXT:::2.8.3.content:
Environmental issues

Emission sources typical of printing processes are:

printing paste residues;
waste water from wash-off and cleaning operations;
volatile organic compounds from drying and fixing.

