Techniques to reduce the energy consumed by stenters and dryers include:

mechanical dewatering of the fabric;
wet-on-wet dyeing or finishing;
optimising exhaust airflow;
insulation;
optimising burner efficiency;
optimised air circulation;
avoiding overdrying;
instrumentation and control of the stenters;
optimal scheduling of the batches;
avoiding loss of latent heat in cylinder dryers;
using high-frequency drying.

