Dry bottom ash treatment combines the techniques of metal separation, size reduction and screening, and may be combined with ageing of the treated bottom ash. The product is a dry aggregate with a controlled grain size (e.g. 0-4 mm, 0-10 mm, 4-10 mm), which may be used as a secondary construction material.

