Wet processes

Wet flue-gas cleaning processes use different types of scrubber design, for example: 

jet scrubbers;
rotation scrubbers;
venturi scrubbers;
dry tower scrubbers;
spray scrubbers;
packed tower scrubbers.

The scrubber solution is (in the case of water-only injection) strongly acidic (typically pH 0-1) due to acids forming in the process of deposition. HCl and Hydrogen Fluoride (HF) are mainly removed in the first stage of the wet scrubber. The effluent from the first stage is recyc

