Effective combustion provides the most important means of reducing emissions to air of organic carbon compounds.

 Flue-gas from waste incineration plants can contain trace quantities of a very wide range of organic species including:

halogenated aromatic hydrocarbons;
polycyclic aromatic hydrocarbons (PAHs);
benzene, toluene and xylene (BTX);
polychlorinated dibenzo-p-dioxins (PCDD) and dibenzofurans (PCDF), (PCDD/F).

PCDD

