The risks associated with the handling of clinical waste can generally be reduced by limiting contact with the waste and by ensuring good storage conditions through the use of:

dedicated containers and the provision of washing/disinfection facilities;
sealed and robust combustible containers, e.g. for sharps and biological hazard materials;
