Wet air oxidation

Description
Wet air oxidation is the reaction of oxygen in the aqueous phase under high pressure and temperature, used to increase the solubility of oxygen in water . The reaction often takes place in the presence of catalysts. Reaction products are dependent on the waste water content and include:

carbon monoxide from organic content;
carbon dioxide from organic content;
water from organic content;
nitrogen from hydrazine, or from ammonia/ammonium and organics which contain

