LVOC:::3.2.1.content:
Process options

The principal options for the production of lower olefins are:

steam cracking;
fluid catalytic cracking;
ethanol dehydration;
propane dehydrogenation;
Fischer-Tropsch conversion of syngas;
methanol-to-olefins.

Of these, the most commonly applied process is steam cracking and this is the only process described in detail in the subsequent sections of this chapter. The others are briefly reviewed below.

