Phosgene-free process for MDI

For the phosgene-free manufacture of MDI, the most viable route has been considered to be a three-step process:

synthesis of methyl phenyl carbamate (Methyl Phenyl Carbamate (MPC)) from aniline and DMC;
condensation of Methyl Phenyl Carbamate (MPC) with formaldehyde to dimethyl methylene diphenyl carbamate (Methylene Diphenyl Carbamate (MDC));
thermal decomposition of Methylene Diphenyl Carbamate (MDC) to MDI (with methanol as a co-product).

